[crates/op-chat-responder/src/main.rs#CCC5]
1://! Guest oneshot chat responder for OP-DBUS.
2://!
3://! The chatbot guest launches exactly one designated turn:
4://! `op-chat-responder --turn-id %i`. This binary opens the guest's mounted
5://! views, reads scoped human input, observes ZeroClaw's selected provider/model,
6://! invokes the unmodified native `threetched.agent` method through mounted FUSE,
7://! then commits through our `chat_response` contract.
8://!
9://! ZeroClaw owns provider selection, model routing, and inference. The
10://! control-plane risk profile is fail-closed unless its only allowed tool is
11://! `delegate`, delegation is explicitly enabled/targeted, and MCP bundles are
12://! absent. Chat history and response accountability remain ours.
13://!
14://! Identity is the live guest kernel binding — not a CLI principal, host MQTT
15://! wake, or D-Bus `ProcessPendingTurn` relay (those paths have no receiver).
16:
